 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Old generic model rows 'Barrel bag', 'Bowling bag', 'Doctor's bag' became the kinds Doctor bag, Bowling bag and Barrel bag; Hermès range 'Kelly' and the Kelly II Sellier/Retourné model rows folded into the Kelly archetype as versions. No Kelly Messenger note was present in the old data, so none carried. Speedy and Alma placed under Bowling bag (alias Boston bag), not Top-handle bag. Gucci Horsebit 1955 left out: sourced pages describe it as a shoulder bag, so it belongs on the Shoulder & crossbody shelf; Jackie likewise. Left out for lack of a retrieved page: Birkin HAC as a version (sources treat it as a separate model), Kelly Pochette/To Go/Danse, Lady Dior size names, Galleria zip variants, Fendi barrel bag, Mulberry/other doctor-bag icons. Purseblog and fortunaauction pages were blocked or empty, not used. Hermès date-stamp eras in Kelly detail come from the Madison Avenue Couture guide (logged)."
}